# File: specs/bug-persist-multi-pr-umbrella-identity-across-child-workflows/feature.gherkin
# Issue: #160

@regression
Feature: Persist umbrella identity across child workflows
  As an nmg-sdlc user delivering an umbrella through child issues
  I want every fresh lifecycle session to reconstruct the same coordination identity
  So that children advance safely without false blockers, resealing loops, or missing siblings

  @regression
  Scenario: Umbrella identity survives a fresh session
    Given a canonical umbrella whose parent has the "epic" label
    And a child has a matching "epic-child-of-N" label, native parent, and body fallback
    When a new lifecycle session hydrates the GitHub records
    Then it classifies the child as a durable member of that parent
    And it does not require ephemeral session state

  @regression
  Scenario: Every lifecycle consumer derives one classification
    Given a child belongs to a persisted umbrella
    When start-issue, write-spec, write-code, verify-code, status, and open-pr inspect it
    Then each consumer uses the shared role, parent, identity, dependency, sibling, and gap fields
    And each derives the same coordination result

  @regression
  Scenario: Genuine dependencies remain blocking
    Given a durable umbrella child also depends on an open non-epic sibling
    When readiness is classified
    Then the coordination parent is excluded from blockers
    And the open sibling remains a named execution dependency
    And unknown or conflicting identity evidence does not make the child ready

  @regression
  Scenario: A canonical child does not reseal the umbrella spec
    Given the refreshed default branch proves the parent specification canonical
    And the active issue is consistently classified as that parent's child
    When write-spec hands off the approved child work
    Then the next stage is write-code for the child
    And no child-numbered seal commit or publication pull request is created

  @regression
  Scenario: Native relationships prevent stale checklist omissions
    Given the native parent has children 201, 202, and 203
    And its checklist names only children 201 and 202
    When sibling-aware delivery evaluates child 201
    Then it uses 202 and 203 as authoritative siblings
    And it reports 203 as missing from the checklist
    And it does not silently omit child 203

  @regression
  Scenario: Legacy umbrella identity is repaired only after exact approval
    Given an upgrade audit finds a parent missing "epic" and a child missing its matching label
    When the operator approves the exact proposed metadata changes
    Then the workflow re-fetches and compares the issue evidence before mutation
    And it applies each approved change once
    And a repeated audit proposes no further change

  @regression
  Scenario: A fresh-session lifecycle fixture remains coordinated end to end
    Given a persisted umbrella fixture with multiple children, a real dependency, and a stale checklist
    When separate planning, start, spec, code, verify, status, and PR-preparation evaluations run
    Then they retain one parent identity across every evaluation
    And they preserve truthful blockers and canonical-spec routing
    And final sibling coordination includes every native child
